			title: "The Induction Matrix"
			x: -7.0d
			y: 3.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000006"]
			description: [
				"&eThermodynamic Conductors&r move &lheat&r - the fourth thing Mekanism pipes, after energy, fluids and gases."
				""
				"&e&lHeat matters for two systems:&r the &7Thermoelectric Boiler&r, which needs heat delivered to boil water, and the &7Fission Reactor&r, which needs heat carried away before it melts down."
				""
				"&c&lThat second one is not optional.&r An under-cooled fission reactor in this pack will destroy your base. Conductors are part of the safety system, not a nicety."
				""
				"&7You can also run them from a Resistive Heater to boil water with pure electricity - inefficient, but it works anywhere and needs no fuel.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:basic_thermodynamic_conductor"
			id: "7ADE000000000007"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000007"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Heat is a resource here"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000700"
				item: "mekanism:basic_thermodynamic_conductor"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Thermodynamic Conductors"
			x: -11.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000016"]
			description: [
				"The &eThermoelectric Boiler&r is a multiblock that turns heat and water into steam. It is half of Mekanism's serious power generation."
				""
				"&e&lThe build:&r a hollow box of Boiler Casing with &7Pressure Disperser&r plates dividing water below from steam above, a &7Superheating Element&r for each heat source, and valves for input and output."
				""
				"&e&lIts output is steam, not power.&r The boiler makes steam; an &7Industrial Turbine&r turns steam into FE. Neither is useful without the other, so plan to build both together."
				""
				"&c&lSize it to your heat source.&r An oversized boiler with two superheating elements produces no more steam than a small one - it just cost more. Check the boiler's stats screen, which tells you its maximum boil rate."
				""
				"&8This is the block your Fission Reactor will feed in Ascension. Building it now with resistive heaters is good practice at low stakes."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:boiler_casing"
			id: "7ADE000000000017"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000017"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Water into steam, at scale"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001700"
				item: "mekanism:boiler_casing"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Thermoelectric Boiler"
			x: -5.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000017"]
			description: [
				"The &eIndustrial Turbine&r is a multiblock that converts steam into Forge Energy - and at full size it produces more power than anything else in the pack short of fusion."
				""
				"&e&lThe build, from the bottom up:&r a Turbine Casing shell, a &7Turbine Rotor&r column up the centre with &7Turbine Blades&r on it, &7Pressure Dispersers&r above, a &7Rotational Complex&r, coils, and vents to release spent steam."
				""
				"&e&lMore blades and more vents means more throughput.&r The turbine's own stats screen tells you its maximum flow rate and whether your vents are limiting it - read it rather than guessing."
				""
				"&c&lVents are the usual bottleneck.&r A turbine that will not hit its rated output almost always needs more vents, not more blades."
				""
				"&7Pair with the boiler above and an Induction Matrix to store the output, and your power problems are over for the rest of the pack.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanismgenerators:turbine_casing"
			id: "7ADE000000000018"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000018"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Steam into serious power"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001800"
				item: "mekanismgenerators:turbine_casing"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Industrial Turbine"
			x: -3.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000018"]
			description: [
				"The &eGas-Burning Generator&r burns combustible gas - most usefully the &7hydrogen&r your Electrolytic Separator is already producing as a by-product."
				""
				"&e&lThis closes a loop you already have open.&r You are splitting water for oxygen to feed the Purification Chamber. The hydrogen half is usually vented or ignored. Feed it here instead and your ore chain part-funds its own power."
				""
				"&e&lIt also burns ethene&r, which the PRC makes from bio fuel - so surplus saplings become electricity through a slightly longer road."
				""
				"&7Buffer the gas with a Chemical Tank. Feeding a generator directly from a separator means both stall whenever either hiccups.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanismgenerators:gas_burning_generator"
			id: "7ADE000000000019"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000019"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Burn hydrogen for power"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001900"
				item: "mekanismgenerators:gas_burning_generator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Gas-Burning Generator"
			x: -1.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6C0C75598D65CE7D"]
			description: [
				"&eWind Generators&r love the void - they scale with altitude, and you live at the top of the sky. Place a field of them high up for cheap, clean Mekanism power."
				""
				"&e&lThis is the one generator a skyblock is actually good at.&r Output scales with Y level, and you start higher than most players ever build. Free real estate."
				""
				"&e&lThe rules that matter:&r"
				"&7- &fOutput rises with altitude.&7 Build them on your highest platform, not at base level."
				"&7- &fThey need open sky.&7 Blocks directly above kill them."
				"&7- &fThey do not need fuel, water, or attention.&7 Ever."
				"&7- &fSome dimensions have no wind at all&7 - do not plan a Moon base around them."
				""
				"&e&lThey are individually weak.&r One will not run a Purification Chamber. The answer is quantity - a field of twenty is trivially cheap, silent, and needs nothing from you again."
				""
				"&7Wire them into an Energy Cube rather than straight to machines. Wind output is steady but small, and the buffer is what turns a trickle into something that can handle a burst of demand.&r"
				""
				"&8Cheap enough to be your first real grid, weak enough that you will still want Powah reactors later. Build both."
			]
			icon: "mekanismgenerators:wind_generator"
			id: "2103000000000005"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2103000000000105"
				type: "xp_levels"
				xp_levels: 3
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Power that scales with height"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2103000000000205"
				item: "mekanismgenerators:wind_generator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Sky Power"
			x: -11.0d
